{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` is **794 LOC** on current `origin/main` (@1c3e945cb8) — 6 under the 800 hard cap the CI module-size gate enforces, i.e. one feature away from breaking the build. Re-measured after tonight's landings — the `staging.py` extraction (267 LOC, owner of the `.tmp-newticket` convention) and the compaction change are already in and did NOT relieve the size pressure. Flagged by audit ae1b.\n\nThe file mixes four independent concerns (full call-graph map in a ticket comment):\n- **A. pre-lock event preparation** — validate the event dict, serialise CANONICAL bytes, hand off to `staging.stage_event`. No lock, no git.\n- **B. bounded / retry-composed git verbs** — every lock-held git child, wall-clock-bounded and composed with gitutil's index.lock + HEAD-parse retries plus a local object-DB retry.\n- **C. commit-failure self-heal** — recover a commit git refused for an unmerged (UU) or poisoned (missing-object) index.\n- **D. locked write orchestration** — the three `lock.write_lock(…, retries=…)` transactions, batch rollback, push / enrich-drain hand-off.\n\n## Approach — extract A and B as leaves; keep C with D\nBehavior-preserving refactor: moved regions stay byte-identical apart from import rebinding, and every relocated name is re-exported from `event_append`, so no consumer, monkeypatch target, or import path changes.\n\n1. **NEW `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py`** (concern A, ~140 LOC) — `EVENT_TYPES`, `StoreError`, `event_filename`, `_ensure_initialized`, `_validate_event`, `_prepare_event`. Owns `canonical_bytes` and the `reducer._version` type-name imports (`KEY_ADD`/`KEY_REVOKE`/`TAG_DELTA`). Composes with `staging.py` rather than duplicating it: `_prepare_event` keeps delegating the `.tmp-newticket` atomic-publish convention to `staging.stage_event`, and its docstring points at `staging.py` instead of restating it. Leaf: imports `staging` + `canonical` only.\n2. **NEW `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`** (concern B, ~220 LOC) — `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_run_git`, `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS`, `_GIT_ADD_ATTEMPTS`, `_GIT_ADD_BACKOFF_S`, `_is_transient_add_error`, `_with_transient_add_retry`, `_git_add`, `_git_commit`, `_git_rm`, `_git_commit_paths`, `_restore_paths`, `_unstage`. Owns `import subprocess` / `import time` and the `# raw-git-ok:` markers, which travel with their functions. Leaf: it **imports** gitutil's shared retry helpers and does **not** edit `gitutil.py` (concurrent work by unheedful-custodial-bluebottle).\n3. **`event_append.py` retains C + D** (~500 LOC, ~300 of cap headroom) — `delete_events`, `stage_and_commit`, `batch_stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `_rollback_batch`, `_maybe_enrich_drain`, `_silent_unlink`, and the self-heal set `_recover_from_unmerged` / `_recover_from_invalid_object` / `_is_invalid_object_error` / `_staged_index_paths` / `_REGENERABLE_PREFIX` / `_INVALID_OBJECT_MARKERS`. Its docstring is retitled to that concern and points at the two new leaves.\n\n### Why C is NOT split out (deliberate seam choice, not incompleteness)\n`_recover_from_invalid_object` and `_recover_from_unmerged` each re-issue `_git_add` on their retry path. `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py::test_own_vanished_object_is_regenerated` performs a SINGLE `monkeypatch.setattr(event_append, \"_git_add\", …)` that today is observed by BOTH `stage_and_commit`'s happy-path add and the recovery re-add, because both resolve `_git_add` through one module global. Moving C to its own module would put those callers in different namespaces and silently decouple that seam. C is also intrinsic to the commit step it heals, so keeping it with D leaves a coherent concern rather than a residue. A and B carry no such coupling.\n\n## Re-export shim — zero test edits, zero consumer edits\nEvery in-repo consumer (`_commands/_seam.py`, `_commands/txn.py`, `_io/import_ndjson.py`, `llm/*/sidecar.py`, `rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py`) and every test reaches these symbols through the `event_append` namespace — in dotted (`event_append.NAME`) and string-literal (`setattr`/`getattr(event_append, \"NAME\")`) forms, enumerated by a two-pass grep over both. `event_append.py` therefore re-exports, with `# noqa: F401`:\n\n- from `event_prepare`: `EVENT_TYPES`, `StoreError`, `event_filename`, `_ensure_initialized`, `_validate_event`, `_prepare_event`\n- from `event_commit_git`: `_run_git`, `_git_add`, `_git_commit`, `_git_rm`, `_git_commit_paths`, `_restore_paths`, `_unstage`, `_is_transient_add_error`, `_with_transient_add_retry`, `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_GIT_ADD_ATTEMPTS`\n- retained: `import subprocess` (kept under `# noqa: F401` — tests patch `event_append.subprocess.run`, and it is the SAME cached module object `event_commit_git` calls, so that seam still reaches the relocated verbs), plus `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S`, `LockTimeout`, `RebaseGuard`, `_lock`.\n\n`event_append` calls the relocated verbs by **bare name** (never `event_commit_git._git_add`) so the module-global lookup stays monkeypatch-visible — this is what preserves the single-`setattr`-reaches-both-callers property above.\n\n## Structural gates checked\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has no `event_append` keys → no path-key churn; `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` sanctions by inline `# raw-git-ok: <reason>` marker with no external allowlist → markers travel with the moved functions.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py::test_opted_in_sites_are_exactly_the_declared_set` asserts `{\"event_append.py\": 3, \"txn.py\": 1, \"push.py\": 1}` — all three `write_lock(retries=…)` sites are in concern D and stay in `event_append.py`, so the per-file count is unchanged.\n- `test_dependency_direction.py` guards `_engine` top-level imports; the new files live under `_store/` and are reached only through `event_append`, so its ALLOWED set is unaffected.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — MODIFY: remove concerns A and B, add the re-export shim, retitle the docstring.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` — NEW (concern A).\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py` — NEW (concern B).\nNo test, consumer, or `gitutil.py` change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` ≤ 560 (from 794; ≥ 240 LOC of headroom under the 800 cap), and every file in `src/rebar/_store/` is ≤ 800.\n- [ ] `event_prepare.py` and `event_commit_git.py` are each ≥ 100 and ≤ 500 LOC and each is a LEAF — neither imports `event_append` nor the other, asserted by both module names being absent from their source, with `python -c \"import rebar._store.event_append\"` succeeding.\n- [ ] Every prior binding resolves unchanged through the `event_append` namespace: `getattr` succeeds on the imported module for each of `stage_and_commit`, `batch_stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `delete_events`, `StoreError`, `EVENT_TYPES`, `event_filename`, `subprocess`, `_run_git`, `_git_add`, `_git_commit`, `_git_rm`, `_git_commit_paths`, `_unstage`, `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_is_transient_add_error`, `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S`, `_maybe_enrich_drain`, `_recover_from_invalid_object`, `_prepare_event`, `_lock`, `LockTimeout`, `RebaseGuard`.\n- [ ] Re-export completeness is a CHECKED invariant over both access forms: with `refs` defined as `{ grep -rhoE 'event_append\\.(_?[A-Za-z_]+)' tests/ src/ --include=*.py | sed 's/^event_append\\.//'; grep -rhoE '(set|get)attr\\(_?[a-z_]*event_append, \"[^\"]+\"' tests/ src/ --include=*.py | sed -E 's/.*\"([^\"]+)\"/\\1/'; } | sort -u`, every name in `refs` is present on the imported `rebar._store.event_append` module object (checked with `getattr`) — no output means no binding was dropped.\n- [ ] Default suite (`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"`) green with **NO edit to any file under `tests/`** — proven by `git diff --name-only origin/main…HEAD` listing only the three `src/rebar/_store/` paths — and `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the `scripts/check_*.py` gates and the generators-no-diff check all clean."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786604995301469001,"uuid":"01dfe18e-05dc-41bd-b40c-39bbeb84fa1e"}